; Take-off range follows the body (22 m, 14 m and 11 m dragons, not three 5 m ones): it is the
; planar distance past which the dragon flies, not a height.
; HoverAltitude is set by the breath, not by the body. The cone is 14 m long and leaves the mouth,
; which rides 4.95 m above the body origin and 4.2 m ahead of it, so at this hover the mouth is
; 3.5 m inside the cone's reach of a standing target's chest and the breath covers about 9.3 m
; around the point under the jaw. Higher than this the air phase cannot touch the ground at all
; (it was cosmetic at the old hover). The body stands 6.3 m tall, so this is a low hover: raising
; it means lengthening the breath's ImpactRadius in data/spells by the same metres.
; The climb speed keeps the climb and the descent at the seconds they always took.
TakeoffRange = 18.0
HoverAltitude = 6.5
ClimbSpeed = 3.25
AirborneDuration = 4.5
GroundedDuration = 8.0
